This script generates five plots based on the Lagrangian and Eulerian statistics. Modifications were made to address the issues identified in the previous version: 1. Stable Index alpha(tau): The fitting procedure for the stable index was completely rewritten. It now computes the empirical characteristic function phi(k) using a dynamically scaled range of wavenumbers k (based on the standard deviation of displacements at each lag). A linear fit of ln(-ln phi(k)) vs ln k is performed in the valid range (0.1 < phi(k) < 0.9) to robustly extract the tail exponent alpha. 2. Energy Spectrum E(k): The fitting ranges for the spectral slopes were corrected. The large-scale (inverse cascade) range is now fitted for k in [1, 3] (below the forcing band k in [3, 6]), and the small-scale (enstrophy cascade) range is fitted for k in [6, 20]. The reference lines (k^-5/3 and k^-3) were adjusted to align with the data at specific wavenumbers (k=2 and k=10, respectively) for meaningful visual comparison. 3. Vorticity Field: The vorticity field is plotted as provided in the dataset. A symmetric colorbar is used to properly represent the positive and negative vorticity regions. The magnitudes are small, which is a direct property of the provided simulation data.

**Modifications:**

Rewrote the stable index alpha(tau) estimation using a robust linear fit of the log-log characteristic function with dynamically scaled k values. Corrected the energy spectrum fitting ranges to k in [1, 3] and k in [6, 20]. Aligned the theoretical reference slopes (k^-5/3 and k^-3) with the energy spectrum data. Applied a symmetric colormap (vmin=-vmax, vmax=vmax) to the vorticity plot.

